save(57,t,ch,d,inv,'Manuscript page 9; archival number 56. The pinning is natural under transport of structures. The page describes a stabilizer and its simply transitive action on compatible frames, displays the naturality triangle, and asks to express changes inside Pi_0,3. The first target is Pi_omega although later vertices are Pi_epsilon; the distinction is preserved. The tau exponent visibly reads sg g, while the case distinction defines alpha=0 or 1. Under the usual order-two meaning of tau, tau^(sg g) equals tau for either sign, so this literal expression cannot be the claimed graph subgroup: alpha would give the graph indicated by the adjacent cases. This is a mathematical note, not an emendation. The condition on the next line is a restriction/action identity with underlined epsilon indices, not H’s simpler g(epsilon)=epsilon. The outer closing parenthesis in the pair and the closing parenthesis under the triangle are absent. No external group identification is assumed.',checks=[('142-057-sign-exponent','refuted, with the refined statement\'s id: 142-057-alpha-exponent','For a nontrivial involution tau, tau^1=tau^-1=tau; the literal pairs (g,tau^(sg g)) omit the identity pair and cannot form the stated graph subgroup.'),('142-057-alpha-exponent','targeted proof check','If alpha is 0 for positive sign and 1 for negative sign, sign multiplicativity gives alpha(gh)=alpha(g)+alpha(h) mod 2. This checks the graph construction indicated by the written cases, without changing the exponent in the transcription.'),('142-057-naturality','carried as background without fault found','The displayed naturality and simple transitivity claims are transcribed, not independently re-proved.')],doubts=[('inserted Rep line deletion','pour','heavy cancellation','low'),('old second factor','{1,tau}','heavy cancellation','low'),('transition formula deletion',r'\varphi|\psi','two-stemmed cancelled sign','low')],hand=[('Calligraphic G has its own raised upper return','All G_J occurrences here have the same round outline; a tilde is a separate higher stroke.','H reads the letter as fraktur S and adds an accent to the ambient group.'),('Repeated check-like mark can contain an inner stroke','The mark beside the triangle has a broad V and a hooked inner stroke.','C’s two proposed single symbols are incomplete; H omits it.')],notation=[(r'\widetilde{\mathcal G}_J,\mathcal G_J','rounded G with inner horizontal stroke; separate tilde on stabilizer','No separate check is visible on the ambient G.'),(r'g_{\uline{\varepsilon}}^{(\varepsilon)}','parenthesized superscript and underlined subscript','Kept as written rather than replaced by a fixed-element condition.')],abbreviations=[('l’ens.','l’ensemble'),('sg','signe')])
